WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.890
Who is lobbying Canadian politicians.

00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:08.363
Two thousand, one hundred and thirty-eight lobbying contacts from a single foreign policy community.

00:00:08.363 --> 00:00:10.579
Ninety-four board nodes.

00:00:10.579 --> 00:00:13.465
One hundred and sixty-nine connections.

00:00:13.465 --> 00:00:18.795
Fifty-eight percent of Canadian MPs lobbied by organized foreign policy interests.

00:00:18.795 --> 00:00:25.363
Six hundred and seventy-eight thousand dollars in sponsored travel to Israel — paid trips for sitting Members of Parliament.

00:00:25.363 --> 00:00:29.170
Anthony Housefather: sixty-seven lobbying contacts.

00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:32.056
Marco Mendicino: sixty-three.

00:00:32.056 --> 00:00:34.431
These are not allegations.

00:00:34.431 --> 00:00:39.181
These are registered communications from the Commissioner of Lobbying's own database.

00:00:39.181 --> 00:00:45.579
Kevin Vuong — the only independent MP to vote no on Vote 658, the foreign power alignment vote.

00:00:45.579 --> 00:00:50.215
Sixty-seven CIJA lobbying contacts directed at one independent member.

00:00:50.215 --> 00:00:53.431
The lobbying machine does not tolerate dissent.

00:00:53.431 --> 00:01:00.363
The foreign agent registry — required by law — remains unproclaimed for over six hundred and fifty-eight days.

00:01:00.363 --> 00:01:03.329
A statutory obligation, breached.

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:07.579
The mechanism that would force transparency... deliberately left dormant.

00:01:07.579 --> 00:01:09.920
The pipeline is documented.

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:20.999
CIJA lobbying contacts map directly to parliamentary votes on IHRA definition adoption, Criminal Code amendments, Human Rights Act civil remedies, arms export permits, and MAID expansion.

00:01:20.999 --> 00:01:22.965
From lobby... to law.

00:01:22.965 --> 00:01:24.999
The data shows the path.

00:01:24.999 --> 00:01:31.147
Three states compete for influence over Canadian policy: the United States, Israel, and China.

00:01:31.147 --> 00:01:35.909
Each uses different mechanisms — lobbying, intelligence, economic leverage.

00:01:35.909 --> 00:01:40.499
All three have documented operations inside Canadian institutions.

00:01:40.499 --> 00:01:44.852
This page shows you who met whom, when, and how they voted afterward.
